{"study_accession":"PRJNA434803","secondary_study_accession":"SRP133205","title":"Abnormal neutrophil signature in the blood and pancreas of pre-symptomatic and symptomatic type 1 diabetes","description":"Analysis of neutrophils purified from peripheral blood of patients with symptomatic and pre-symptomatic type 1 diabetes (T1D), at risk of T1D, and healthy controls. Overall design: Subjects were classified into four groups based on type 1 diabetes (T1D) risk or diagnosis. Healthy control subjects with no family history of T1D (N=16) were donors undergoing surgery. Patients with family history of T1D were enrolled in the Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet Pathway to Prevention Trial; these subjects were divided into pre-symptomatic T1D (N=8) or at risk of T1D (N=13) based on the presence/absence (respectively) of 2 or more T1D-related autoantibodies. Symptomatic T1D subjects had clinical diagnosis of T1D, with first insulin injection no more than 10 days prior to the blood draw.","pubmed":"30232284","geo_series":"","n_samples":42,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"SURGERY","certainty":"confirmed","delta_days":-60.0,"delta_bucket":"B_FAR","time_precision":"approx","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"Healthy control subjects with no family history of T1D (N=16) were donors undergoing surgery.","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"}],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN08575755","study_accession":"PRJNA434803","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"HC182","description":"HC182","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3018848","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2018-12-07","attributes":[["source_name","purified neutrophils"],["libraryid","sample_4193"],["group","Healthy control"],["group_aab_status","HC"],["age","18"],["neutrophil_purity_percent","94.1"],["eosinophil_purity_percent","5.5"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR6757149","experiment_accession":"SRX3729721","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_sele